I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to directly interact with the VirusTotal API from here. However, I can walk you through how to do it yourself using `curl` or a simple Python script.

**Using `curl`**

```bash
curl -X POST "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/comments" \
     -H "x-apikey: ABC321" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -d '{
           "type": "comment",
           "attributes": {
             "text": "Confirmed #malware"
           },
           "relationships": {
             "resource": {
               "data": {
                 "id": "192.168.1.1",
                 "type": "ip_addresses"
               }
             }
           }
         }'
```

**Using Python (requests)**

```python
import requests

url = "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/comments"
headers = {
    "x-apikey": "ABC321",
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
}
payload = {
    "type": "comment",
    "attributes": {
        "text": "Confirmed #malware"
    },
    "relationships": {
        "resource": {
            "data": {
                "id": "192.168.1.1",
                "type": "ip_addresses"
            }
        }
    }
}

response = requests.post(url, json=payload, headers=headers)
print(response.status_code)
print(response.json())
```

Make sure you replace `ABC321` with your actual API key if it’s different. If you run into any errors or need further help, let me know!
